    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="meta">Effective November 5, 2026 · Applies to the Branch Chat Chrome extension</p>
    <p class="lead">Branch Chat lets you highlight text in an AI chat and open a side conversation about it. This policy explains what the extension reads, where that information is kept, and where it is sent.</p>
  </header>

  <aside class="glance" aria-label="Summary">
    <h2>At a glance</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><span>Branch Chat has no servers of its own. The developer never receives your chats, questions, images or keys.</span></li>
      <li><span>Everything is stored in your own browser. It is sent only to the AI provider you choose, when you send a branch message.</span></li>
      <li><span>No analytics, no tracking, no advertising, and no sale of data.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </aside>

  <section aria-labelledby="reads">
    <h2 id="reads">What the extension reads and stores</h2>
    <p>Branch Chat only reads a page when you act: when you right-click selected text and choose <strong>Branch chat</strong>, or press <strong>Update</strong> in a branch.</p>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Information</th><th scope="col">Why</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>The text you highlight</td><td>It is the subject of the branch.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>The visible conversation on ChatGPT, Claude or Gemini</td><td>So a branch can remember the chat it came from. You can turn this off in Account → Answer preferences.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>The questions you type and images you attach in branches</td><td>They make up the branch conversation.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>The address and title of the chat tab</td><td>So branches are saved with, and shown for, the right chat.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>The name you enter during setup</td><td>Shown in the extension only.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Your AI provider API key, or the key created by Sign in with OpenRouter</td><td>Needed to send requests to that provider on your behalf.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Your settings</td><td>Chosen provider, model and answer preferences.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>All of this is stored locally with Chrome's extension storage (<code>chrome.storage.local</code>) on your device. It is not synced to other devices and is deleted when you remove the extension.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="sent">
    <h2 id="sent">What is sent, and to whom</h2>
    <p>When you send a message in a branch, Branch Chat sends a request directly from your browser to the one AI provider you selected. That request contains:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>the copy of the original chat (unless you turned that off),</li>
      <li>the highlighted text and the messages and images in that branch and the branches above it,</li>
      <li>your API key, to authenticate with that provider.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The provider handles that data under its own privacy policy:
      <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/legal/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Anthropic</a>,
      <a href="https://openai.com/policies/privacy-policy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">OpenAI</a>,
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google</a>,
      <a href="https://openrouter.ai/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">OpenRouter</a>.
      If you connect your own custom server, requests go only to the address you entered.</p>
    <p><strong>Sign in with OpenRouter</strong> opens OpenRouter's own sign-in page. After you approve, OpenRouter returns an API key, which is stored only in your browser.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="not">
    <h2 id="not">What Branch Chat does not do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>It does not collect your browsing history, and it does not read pages you have not chosen to branch from.</li>
      <li>It does not log keystrokes, clicks or other activity.</li>
      <li>It does not include analytics, crash reporting, advertising or tracking code.</li>
      <li>It does not sell, rent or share your data with anyone other than the AI provider you choose.</li>
      <li>It does not use your data for advertising, or to determine creditworthiness or for lending.</li>
      <li>It does not run code downloaded from the internet. All code ships inside the extension.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The use of information received by Branch Chat adheres to the <a href="https://developer.chrome.com/docs/webstore/program-policies/user-data-faq" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Chrome Web Store User Data Policy</a>, including the Limited Use requirements.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="choices">
    <h2 id="choices">Your choices</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Delete branches:</strong> hover a branch and press ×, or delete a whole chat from History.</li>
      <li><strong>Disconnect a provider:</strong> Account → Disconnect removes its key from your browser.</li>
      <li><strong>Sign out:</strong> removes your account name and all keys; branches remain until you delete them.</li>
      <li><strong>Stop sending the original chat:</strong> turn off "Remember the original chat" in Answer preferences.</li>
      <li><strong>Remove everything:</strong> uninstalling the extension deletes all of its stored data. Use Export backup first if you want a copy.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="kids">
    <h2 id="kids">Children</h2>
    <p>Branch Chat is not directed to children under 13 and does not knowingly collect information from them.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="changes">
    <h2 id="changes">Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>If what the extension does with your data changes, this page will be updated and the effective date above will change.</p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="contact">
    <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about this policy can be sent to the developer through the contact details on Branch Chat's Chrome Web Store listing.</p>
  </section>

  <footer>Branch Chat · Privacy Policy · Effective November 5, 2026</footer>
